# Optional. Where the browser can reach Stooq's CSV quote endpoint.
#
# Stooq sends no CORS headers, so the page cannot call it directly — the
# request has to go through a proxy. Left unset, the app uses /api/stooq,
# which the Vite dev server proxies (vite.config.ts) and netlify.toml
# forwards on a deployed build. That covers both normal setups; set this
# only if you host the proxy somewhere else.
#
# An absolute URL works too, provided that host sends CORS headers.
# VITE_STOOQ_PROXY=/api/stooq

# Exchange rates (Frankfurter) and instrument lookup (OpenFIGI) need no
# configuration and no API key — they are CORS-enabled and called directly.
